  "rationale": "All three columns centre on one coherent, data-inferable focus: characterising the patient's presenting concern. concern_type supplies the primary typology directly answering the query, while clinical_domain and visit_stage_in_continuum form complementary, non-redundant facets (clinical area and position in the care continuum) at a useful granularity. There is minor conceptual overlap between the acute/chronic/follow-up values of concern_type and visit_stage_in_continuum, which slightly weakens differentiation, but they are distinct enough to constitute a sound analytical structure rather than a restatement. The implied focus is clearly actionable: an analyst can profile and segment the dominant concern types (e.g., the large acute_diagnosis share) across domains and care stages to investigate demand patterns. This is not a mechanical/generic set, so the claim is well realised."
}
